> Address ║ 0.0.0.0:8480_   ╔═ Webhook receiver ═══════════════════════════════════════════╗                           ║
          ╚═════════════════║ ⚠ Let the webhook receiver listen on 0.0.0.0:8480?           ║═══════════════════════════╝
          host:port with a p║                                                              ║                            
                            ║ The receiver restarts on the new address. The hooks stay as  ║                            
                            ║ they are. The address is not local and the receiver speaks   ║                            
                            ║ plain HTTP: a reverse proxy should provide HTTPS.            ║                            
                            ║ $ sudo qhost hook-service setup --listen 0.0.0.0:8480        ║                            
                            ║   --confirm --yes --output json                              ║                            
                            ║                                                              ║                            
                            ║ [ yes, with sudo ]  > cancel <                               ║                            
